  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A person invites a party of 10 friends at dinner and place them so that 4 are on one round table and 6 on the other round table. The number of ways in which he can arrange the guests is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "yqqXY",
      "text": "$\\frac{(10) !}{6 !}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "RHGD2",
      "text": "$\\frac{(10) !}{24}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "BG9FH",
      "text": "$\\frac{(9) !}{24}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "LcDNd",
      "text": "None of these",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Selection of 6 guests $=10 \\mathrm{C} 6$ \r\n\r\nPermutation of 6 on round table $=5 !$ \r\n\r\nPermutation of 4 on round table $=3 !$\r\n\r\nThen, total number of arrangements $=10 \\mathrm{C} 6.5 ! .3 !$\r\n\r\n$=\\frac{(10) !}{6 ! 4 !} \\cdot 5 ! .3 !=\\frac{(10) !}{24}$",
    "image": null
  },
